questions.question:
If the solution curve y = y(x) of the differential equation \((1+y^2)(1+\log_{e} x)dx + x dy = 0, x > 0\) passes through the point (1, 1) and
y(e) = \frac{\alpha - \tan(\frac{3}{2})}{\beta + \tan(\frac{3}{2})}
then \(\alpha + 2\beta\) is _______.

questions.explanation:
\int (\frac{1}{x} + \frac{\ln x}{x}) dx + \int \frac{dy}{1+y^2} = 0
\ln x + \frac{(\ln x)^2}{2} + \tan^{-1} y = C
Put x = 1, y = 1
C = \frac{\pi}{4}
\Rightarrow \ln x + \frac{(\ln x)^2}{2} + \tan^{-1} y = \frac{\pi}{4}
Put x = e
y = \tan(\frac{\pi}{4} - \frac{3}{2}) = \frac{1 - \tan \frac{3}{2}}{1 + \tan \frac{3}{2}}
\alpha = 1, \beta = 1
\Rightarrow \alpha + 2\beta = 3

